%N A399109 Sum of the cubes of the coefficients of (x + y + 2*z)^n.
%C A399109 Equivalently, a(n) counts colored Abelian cubes of block length n over three underlying letters, where the third letter has two colors. Also, a(n)/64^n is the probability that three independent Multinomial(n; 1/4, 1/4, 1/2) random vectors are equal.
%H A399109 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A399109/a399109.pdf">Sums of Powers of Coefficients: Formulas, Sequences and Interpretations</a>.
%H A399109 Guy Louchard and Mark Daniel Ward, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10653106">Asymptotic Analysis of Sums of Powers of Multinomial Coefficients: A Saddle Point Approach</a>, Integers 17 (2017), Art. A47.
%H A399109 L. B. Richmond and Jeffrey Shallit, <a href="https://www.combinatorics.org/ojs/index.php/eljc/article/view/v16i1r72">Counting Abelian Squares</a>, Electron. J. Combin. 16 (2009), Art. R72. See also <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/:0807.5028">arXiv:0807.5028</a> [math.CO], 2008.
%F A399109 a(n) = Sum_{i+j+k=n} (n!/(i!*j!*k!))^3 * 8^k.
%F A399109 a(n) = Sum_{r=0..n} binomial(n,r)^3 * Sum_{k=0..r} binomial(r,k)^3 * 8^k.
%F A399109 Normalized generating function: Sum_{n>=0} a(n)*x^n/(n!)^3 = _0F_2(;1,1;x)^2 * _0F_2(;1,1;8*x).
%e A399109 For n=1, the coefficients of x + y + 2*z are 1, 1, 2, so a(1) = 1^3 + 1^3 + 2^3 = 10.
%p A399109 a := n -> add(binomial(n,r)^3 * add(binomial(r,k)^3 * 8^k, k=0..r), r=0..n);
%Y A399109 Cf. A002893 (sum of squares of the coefficients of (x+y+z)^n), A141057 (sum of cubes of the coefficients of (x+y+z)^n).
%K A399109 nonn,easy,new
%O A399109 0,2
